{"type":"message","id":"d9f739b6","parentId":"54c50d24","timestamp":"2026-03-14T05:11:49.747Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"async function kimiSearch(query, apiKey = 'sk-CwQYlNUFoRTFzk3sPT2cte9y3lsZ3aqRcot2RAiHTqi2AnUN') {\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch('https://api.moonshot.cn/v1/chat/completions', {\n      method: 'POST',\n      headers: {\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n        'Authorization': `Bearer ${apiKey}`\n      },\n      body: JSON.stringify({\n        model: 'moonshot-v1-8k',\n        messages: [{ role: 'user', content: query }],\n        stream: false,\n        use_search: true\n      })\n    });\n\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      throw new Error(`API error: ${response.status} ${response.statusText}`);\n    }\n\n    const data = await response.json();\n    const answer = data.choices[0].message.content;\n    return answer;\n  } catch (error) {\n    return `搜索失败: ${error.message}`;\n  }\n}\n\nmodule.exports = kimiSearch;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773465109744}}
{"type":"message","id":"d1914df1","parentId":"d9f739b6","timestamp":"2026-03-14T05:11:59.902Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec:2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/yankeeting/.openclaw/workspace && node -e \"\nconst kimiSearch = require('./kimi_search.js');\n\nasync function search() {\n  console.log('=== 搜索关键词1: AI Agent delegation subagent best practices ===');\n  const result1 = await kimiSearch('AI Agent delegation subagent best practices why delegate instead of direct execution');\n  console.log(result1);\n  console.log('\\n\\n=== 搜索关键词2: 如何避免 AI 自己直接执行任务 ===');\n  const result2 = await kimiSearch('如何避免 AI 自己直接执行任务 委派给 subagent');\n  console.log(result2);\n  console.log('\\n\\n=== 搜索关键词3: AI agent 委派任务给 subagent ===');\n  const result3 = await kimiSearch('AI agent 委派任务给 subagent 什么情况下应该委派');\n  console.log(result3);\n}\n\nsearch().catch(console.error);\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"volces-com","model":"ark-code-latest","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773465109747}}
{"type":"message","id":"a317cbc6","parentId":"d1914df1","timestamp":"2026-03-14T05:12:23.625Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"exec:2","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== 搜索关键词1: AI Agent delegation subagent best practices ===\nDelegating tasks to a subagent instead of directly executing them can be beneficial in various scenarios, especially when dealing with complex systems or large-scale operations. Here are some best practices and reasons for delegating tasks to a subagent:\n\n1. **Specialization and Expertise**: Subagents can be designed with specific expertise or specialized skills that are not present in the main AI agent. This allows for more efficient and effective task completion.\n\n2. **Scalability**: Delegating tasks can help scale operations by distributing workload across multiple subagents, which can operate in parallel, thus improving overall system performance.\n\n3. **Fault Tolerance**: If a subagent fails, the main AI agent can continue to function, and the failed task can be reassigned to another subagent, reducing the risk of system-wide failure.\n\n4. **Resource Management**: Subagents can help manage resources more effectively by focusing on specific tasks, allowing the main AI agent to allocate resources where they are most needed.\n\n5. **Modularity**: Delegating tasks promotes a modular system design, which makes it easier to update, maintain, and debug individual components without affecting the entire system.\n\n6. **Task Complexity**: For complex tasks that require multiple steps or involve different types of expertise, delegating to subagents can simplify the process and make it more manageable.\n\n7. **Response Time**: Subagents can be designed to respond quickly to specific types of requests or tasks, improving the overall response time of the system.\n\n8. **Security**: By delegating certain tasks, the main AI agent can maintain a higher level of security, as sensitive operations can be handled by trusted subagents with appropriate security protocols.\n\n9. **Adaptability**: Subagents can be more easily adapted to changing conditions or requirements, allowing the system to evolve and respond to new challenges.\n\n10. **Cost-Effectiveness**: Delegating tasks can be more cost-effective, as it allows for the use of specialized subagents that are only active when needed, rather than having a single, more expensive AI agent that must handle all tasks.\n\n11. **Human-AI Interaction**: In cases where tasks involve human interaction, subagents can be designed to handle specific types of interactions, improving user experience and satisfaction.\n\n12. **Compliance and Legal Considerations**: Delegating certain tasks to subagents can help ensure compliance with legal and regulatory requirements, as each subagent can be tailored to meet specific standards.\n\nIn summary, delegating tasks to subagents can lead to a more efficient, robust, and adaptable AI system. It allows for specialization, better resource management, and improved system performance, while also providing benefits in terms of fault tolerance, security, and compliance.\n\n\n=== 搜索关键词2: 如何避免 AI 自己直接执行任务 ===\n要避免人工智能（AI）直接执行任务，而是将其委派给子代理（subagent），可以采取以下步骤：\n\n1. **明确角色和职责**：\n   - 定义AI的主要角色，即作为协调者或决策支持系统，而不是执行者。\n   - 确定哪些任务需要委派给子代理，以及这些子代理的职责和权限。\n\n2. **建立通信协议**：\n   - 设计一套通信协议，确保AI能够与子代理进行有效的信息交换。\n   - 确保AI能够发送任务指令，并接收子代理的反馈和状态更新。\n\n3. **任务分配机制**：\n   - 开发一个任务分配系统，AI可以通过这个系统将任务分配给最合适的子代理。\n   - 这个系统应该能够根据任务的性质、子代理的能力、资源的可用性等因素来做出决策。\n\n4. **监控和控制**：\n   - 实施监控机制，以跟踪子代理的任务执行情况。\n   - 设计控制机制，以便在必要时AI可以介入或调整任务分配。\n\n5. **反馈和学习**：\n   - 建立反馈循环，使AI能够从子代理的任务执行结果中学习。\n   - 利用机器学习技术，不断优化任务分配策略和子代理的执行效率。\n\n6. **安全和合规性**：\n   - 确保所有任务分配和执行都符合安全和合规性要求。\n   - 对子代理的行为进行审计，以确保它们的行为符合既定的规则和标准。\n\n7. **用户界面和交互**：\n   - 如果AI系统与人类用户交互，设计直观的用户界面，让用户能够轻松地理解AI的决策和子代理的任务执行情况。\n   - 提供用户干预的选项，以便在需要时可以手动调整任务分配。\n\n8. **测试和验证**：\n   - 在实际部署之前，对AI和子代理的交互进行广泛的测试和验证。\n   - 确保系统在各种情况下都能稳定运行，并能够处理异常情况。\n\n通过这些步骤，可以确保AI系统不会直接执行任务，而是有效地将任务委派给子代理，同时保持对整个流程的控制和监督。\n\n\n=== 搜索关键词3: AI agent 委派任务给 subagent ===\nAI代理（AI agent）委派任务给子代理（subagent）通常在以下情况下是合适的：\n\n1. **任务复杂性**：当任务过于复杂，需要多个步骤或专业知识时，将任务分解并委派给不同的子代理可以提高效率和准确性。\n\n2. **资源分配**：如果AI代理需要同时处理多个任务，而资源（如计算能力、存储空间或时间）有限，委派部分任务给子代理可以帮助更有效地管理资源。\n\n3. **专业化**：当任务需要特定领域的专业知识时，委派给专门处理该领域任务的子代理可以提高任务执行的质量。\n\n4. **地理位置**：如果任务需要在特定地理位置执行，而AI代理无法直接访问该位置，委派给地理位置更合适的子代理是合理的。\n\n5. **时间敏感性**：对于需要快速响应的任务，委派给能够立即行动的子代理可以减少延迟。\n\n6. **风险管理**：在某些情况下，将任务委派给子代理可以帮助分散风险，特别是在处理可能失败或需要备份计划的任务时。\n\n7. **合规性和法律要求**：在需要遵守特定法律或合规要求的情况下，委派给了解这些要求的子代理可以确保任务的合法性。\n\n8. **成本效益**：如果委派任务给子代理可以降低成本，例如通过利用更便宜的劳动力或资源，这可能是一个合理的选择。\n\n9. **学习和适应**：AI代理可能委派任务给子代理以收集数据和经验，从而学习和改进其自身的性能。\n\n10. **用户偏好**：如果用户对特定任务有特定的代理偏好，AI代理可能会委派任务以满足这些偏好。\n\n在委派任务时，AI代理需要考虑任务的性质、可用资源、子代理的能力以及最终目标，以确保任务能够以最有效的方式完成。"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":23720,"aggregated":"=== 搜索关键词1: AI Agent delegation subagent best practices ===\nDelegating tasks to a subagent instead of directly executing them can be beneficial in various scenarios, especially when dealing with complex systems or large-scale operations. Here are some best practices and reasons for delegating tasks to a subagent:\n\n1. **Specialization and Expertise**: Subagents can be designed with specific expertise or specialized skills that are not present in the main AI agent. This allows for more efficient and effective task completion.\n\n2. **Scalability**: Delegating tasks can help scale operations by distributing workload across multiple subagents, which can operate in parallel, thus improving overall system performance.\n\n3. **Fault Tolerance**: If a subagent fails, the main AI agent can continue to function, and the failed task can be reassigned to another subagent, reducing the risk of system-wide failure.\n\n4. **Resource Management**: Subagents can help manage resources more effectively by focusing on specific tasks, allowing the main AI agent to allocate resources where they are most needed.\n\n5. **Modularity**: Delegating tasks promotes a modular system design, which makes it easier to update, maintain, and debug individual components without affecting the entire system.\n\n6. **Task Complexity**: For complex tasks that require multiple steps or involve different types of expertise, delegating to subagents can simplify the process and make it more manageable.\n\n7. **Response Time**: Subagents can be designed to respond quickly to specific types of requests or tasks, improving the overall response time of the system.\n\n8. **Security**: By delegating certain tasks, the main AI agent can maintain a higher level of security, as sensitive operations can be handled by trusted subagents with appropriate security protocols.\n\n9. **Adaptability**: Subagents can be more easily adapted to changing conditions or requirements, allowing the system to evolve and respond to new challenges.\n\n10. **Cost-Effectiveness**: Delegating tasks can be more cost-effective, as it allows for the use of specialized subagents that are only active when needed, rather than having a single, more expensive AI agent that must handle all tasks.\n\n11. **Human-AI Interaction**: In cases where tasks involve human interaction, subagents can be designed to handle specific types of interactions, improving user experience and satisfaction.\n\n12. **Compliance and Legal Considerations**: Delegating certain tasks to subagents can help ensure compliance with legal and regulatory requirements, as each subagent can be tailored to meet specific standards.\n\nIn summary, delegating tasks to subagents can lead to a more efficient, robust, and adaptable AI system. It allows for specialization, better resource management, and improved system performance, while also providing benefits in terms of fault tolerance, security, and compliance.\n\n\n=== 搜索关键词2: 如何避免 AI 自己直接执行任务 ===\n要避免人工智能（AI）直接执行任务，而是将其委派给子代理（subagent），可以采取以下步骤：\n\n1. **明确角色和职责**：\n   - 定义AI的主要角色，即作为协调者或决策支持系统，而不是执行者。\n   - 确定哪些任务需要委派给子代理，以及这些子代理的职责和权限。\n\n2. **建立通信协议**：\n   - 设计一套通信协议，确保AI能够与子代理进行有效的信息交换。\n   - 确保AI能够发送任务指令，并接收子代理的反馈和状态更新。\n\n3. **任务分配机制**：\n   - 开发一个任务分配系统，AI可以通过这个系统将任务分配给最合适的子代理。\n   - 这个系统应该能够根据任务的性质、子代理的能力、资源的可用性等因素来做出决策。\n\n4. **监控和控制**：\n   - 实施监控机制，以跟踪子代理的任务执行情况。\n   - 设计控制机制，以便在必要时AI可以介入或调整任务分配。\n\n5. **反馈和学习**：\n   - 建立反馈循环，使AI能够从子代理的任务执行结果中学习。\n   - 利用机器学习技术，不断优化任务分配策略和子代理的执行效率。\n\n6. **安全和合规性**：\n   - 确保所有任务分配和执行都符合安全和合规性要求。\n   - 对子代理的行为进行审计，以确保它们的行为符合既定的规则和标准。\n\n7. **用户界面和交互**：\n   - 如果AI系统与人类用户交互，设计直观的用户界面，让用户能够轻松地理解AI的决策和子代理的任务执行情况。\n   - 提供用户干预的选项，以便在需要时可以手动调整任务分配。\n\n8. **测试和验证**：\n   - 在实际部署之前，对AI和子代理的交互进行广泛的测试和验证。\n   - 确保系统在各种情况下都能稳定运行，并能够处理异常情况。\n\n通过这些步骤，可以确保AI系统不会直接执行任务，而是有效地将任务委派给子代理，同时保持对整个流程的控制和监督。\n\n\n=== 搜索关键词3: AI agent 委派任务给 subagent ===\nAI代理（AI agent）委派任务给子代理（subagent）通常在以下情况下是合适的：\n\n1. **任务复杂性**：当任务过于复杂，需要多个步骤或专业知识时，将任务分解并委派给不同的子代理可以提高效率和准确性。\n\n2. **资源分配**：如果AI代理需要同时处理多个任务，而资源（如计算能力、存储空间或时间）有限，委派部分任务给子代理可以帮助更有效地管理资源。\n\n3. **专业化**：当任务需要特定领域的专业知识时，委派给专门处理该领域任务的子代理可以提高任务执行的质量。\n\n4. **地理位置**：如果任务需要在特定地理位置执行，而AI代理无法直接访问该位置，委派给地理位置更合适的子代理是合理的。\n\n5. **时间敏感性**：对于需要快速响应的任务，委派给能够立即行动的子代理可以减少延迟。\n\n6. **风险管理**：在某些情况下，将任务委派给子代理可以帮助分散风险，特别是在处理可能失败或需要备份计划的任务时。\n\n7. **合规性和法律要求**：在需要遵守特定法律或合规要求的情况下，委派给了解这些要求的子代理可以确保任务的合法性。\n\n8. **成本效益**：如果委派任务给子代理可以降低成本，例如通过利用更便宜的劳动力或资源，这可能是一个合理的选择。\n\n9. **学习和适应**：AI代理可能委派任务给子代理以收集数据和经验，从而学习和改进其自身的性能。\n\n10. **用户偏好**：如果用户对特定任务有特定的代理偏好，AI代理可能会委派任务以满足这些偏好。\n\n在委派任务时，AI代理需要考虑任务的性质、可用资源、子代理的能力以及最终目标，以确保任务能够以最有效的方式完成。","cwd":"/home/yankeeting/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773465143623}}
{"type":"message","id":"fd017329","parentId":"a317cbc6","timestamp":"2026-03-14T05:13:03.608Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## 🔍 搜索结果摘要\n\n基于 kimi_search.js 的搜索结果，我整理出了关于 **\"AI Agent 如何遵守规则、避免自己直接干活，而应该委派给 Subagent\"** 的完整答案：\n\n---\n\n### 1️⃣ 为什么 AI 应该委派而不是自己执行？\n\n| 原因 | 说明 |\n|------|------|\n| **专业化** | Subagent 可以设计为特定领域的专家，执行效率更高 |\n| **可扩展性** | 任务并行分发到多个 Subagent，提升整体性能 |\n| **容错性** | 单个 Subagent 失败不影响主 Agent，任务可重新分配 |\n| **资源管理** | 按需分配计算资源，避免主 Agent 过载 |\n| **模块化** | 独立维护、更新、调试各组件，不影响整体系统 |\n| **响应时间** | Subagent 可针对特定任务优化响应速度 |\n| **安全性** | 敏感操作可委托给受信任的 Subagent 处理 |\n| **成本效益** | 按需激活专用 Subagent，避免全天候高成本运行 |\n\n---\n\n### 2️⃣ 什么情况下应该委派？\n\n**应该委派的情况：**\n\n| 场景 | 示例 |\n|------|------|\n| **任务复杂** | 需要多个步骤、专业知识或多领域协作的任务 |\n| **资源受限** | 主 Agent 需要同时处理多个任务，计算/时间/存储不足 |\n| **需要专业领域知识** | 代码审查、数学计算、法律分析等专业领域 |\n| **地理位置限制** | 任务需要在特定网络/服务器/位置执行 |\n| **时间敏感** | 需要快速响应，Subagent 可立即行动 |\n| **风险分散** | 处理可能失败的任务，需要备份计划 |\n| **合规性要求** | 需要遵守特定法律/监管标准的任务 |\n| **成本优化** | 利用更便宜的计算资源或专用服务 |\n| **用户偏好** | 用户对特定任务有指定的代理偏好 |\n\n**不应该委派的情况：**\n\n- 简单读取操作（<10秒可完成）\n- 用户直接询问的简单事实查询\n- 需要主 Agent 直接响应的实时交互\n\n---\n\n### 3️⃣ 如何确保遵守这个规则？\n\n| 措施 | 具体做法 |\n|------|---------|\n| **明确定义角色职责** | 主 Agent 是协调者/决策者，不是执行者；明确哪些任务必须委派 |\n| **建立通信协议** | 设计标准接口，确保主 Agent 能向 Subagent 发送指令并接收反馈 |\n| **任务分配机制** | 根据任务性质、Subagent 能力、资源可用性自动决策分配 |\n| **监控和控制** | 实时跟踪 Subagent 执行状态，必要时主 Agent 介入调整 |\n| **反馈学习** | 从 Subagent 执行结果中学习，持续优化任务分配策略 |\n| **安全和合规** | 所有委派行为符合安全和合规要求，审计 Subagent 行为 |\n| **用户界面** | 让用户理解主 Agent 的决策和 Subagent 的执行状态 |\n| **测试验证** | 部署前广泛测试主 Agent 与 Subagent 的交互，确保各种场景稳定运行 |\n\n---\n\n### 📌 总结\n\n**核心原则：**\n\n> 主 Agent 是 **大脑** 🧠 —— 负责决策、协调、监督\n> Subagent 是 **手脚** 🦾 —— 负责执行、专业处理、并行工作\n\n**简单记忆口诀：**\n\n| 情况 | 谁来执行 |\n|------|---------|\n| 简单读取（<10秒） | 主 Agent 直接执行 |\n| 搜索/收集信息 | 委派给 Explorer Subagent |\n| 修改文件/运行命令 | 委派给 Executor Subagent |\n| 耗时操作（>10秒） | 委派给 Executor Subagent |\n| 批量处理 | 委派给 Executor Subagent |\n\n这就是 **\"Orchestrator 模式\"** —— 主 Agent 只做编排，不做苦力！ 🦞"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"volces-com","model":"ark-code-latest","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773465143624}}
